# Quicksave — UnitySolarSystem: living multi-system sim (Alpha Centauri, rings, avoidance, free ships)
_Printed: 2026-10-11_

## Current task
Nothing is mid-edit. Everything is committed and pushed to `main` (latest `c8e4375`). Resume by asking the owner for the next feature.

Standing owner direction for every new feature: "make sure this is a simulation, not a static clockwork with no room for freedom and adjustment". Ships should notice and react: avoid collisions, roam freely, change their minds mid-flight. Prefer stateful, reactive agent behaviour layered over the analytic Kepler/brachistochrone schedules.

## Decisions locked this session
- **Docking rings:**
  - Rings hover directly over cities (powered station-keeping, labelled fiction) at the stationary-orbit radius, else 3 radii.
  - Earth has 7 rings: New York, Paris, Beijing, Tokyo, Sydney, Johannesburg, Moscow.
  - Mars has 2 (Jezero, Tharsis); Venus and Titan have 1 each; Proxima b has 2 (Dawn and Dusk on the terminator).
  - Only merchants and couriers land (`IsTrader`); warships and pirates hold orbit.
- **Alpha Centauri candidates:** S1 ("Alpha Centauri Ab") is included as a CANDIDATE and Proxima c as DISPUTED; both are labelled.
- **Out of scope until asked:** interstellar ship travel. Only the camera travels between systems (StarTravel).
- **Satellite constellations** are OFF by default; the K key toggles them.
- **Ship plating:** CC0 ambientCG MetalPlates015A, applied triplanar in Ship.shader, packed into `Resources/Textures/ship_plating.png` (R = detail, GB = normal). Factions are told apart by hull shading.
- **Space** is an eased pause (×0.99 per step at 120 steps/s down to 1%, then 0; it resumes the same way). Up/down movement moved to Q/E or C/].
- **R / LEVEL button** smoothly levels the view to the system plane (ecliptic in Sol, A–B orbit in Alpha Centauri). A new system starts with the ecliptic level.
- **Economy** stays at full complexity (owner: easier to dial down than to build up).
- **Commits:** only when the owner asks (`/commit` also pushes). Footer:
  - `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`
  - `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017GEbVV7vbX7qjt2TdN9AmZ`
- Never stage `.claude/worktrees/`; it belongs to another session.

