## Open questions / pending
- **Miranda (1.7°), Enceladus (0.45°) and Deimos (0.37°)** errors are inherent to the mean-orbit model. Improving them needs periodic perturbation terms; not requested.
- **Ship sidesteps are only km-scale,** so they're barely visible at gameplay zoom. Possibly make avoidance visible, if the owner wants it.
- **Further "simulation not clockwork" ideas,** not yet built:
  - convoys re-routing around dangerous lanes mid-journey;
  - pirates intercepting merchants in open space;
  - free ships reacting to battles (fleeing or spectating);
  - traders replanning when a market changes mid-trip.
- **A fresh `-demo -capture video hq` recording** may be wanted to show the latest work.

## Next concrete steps
